<title>USA: G7 believes Russian economy has bottomed-Rexrodt.</title>
<headline>G7 believes Russian economy has bottomed-Rexrodt.</headline>
<dateline>DENVER 1997-06-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Group of Seven industrialized nations believes that Russia's economy has now bottomed out, German economics minister Guenter Rexrodt said at a breakfast briefing on Saturday.</p>
<p>&quot;The general impression is that the Russian economy has reached its trough,&quot; Rexrodt said.</p>
<p>Rexrodt was speaking on the sidelines of the summit meeting of top politicians from the G7 countries. The G7 comprises Britain, Canada, France, Germany, Italy, Japan and the United States. Russia, for the first time, been invited to attend almost every session of the annual summit meeting.</p>
<p>((--Janet Northcote, Summit newsroom +1 303 454 8244))</p>
